          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            (a category with all finite limits), then it is interesting to consider a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (a functor that preserves all
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            lacks some finite limits, then this concept still makes sense, but it may not be the correct one. Instead we use the stronger concept of a
            = succeed "," do
              %em flat functor
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            It turns out that the most appropriate generality in which to speak of a flat functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to D
            is when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %h3#valued_functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            \-valued functors
          %p The most classical notion is the following.
          #SetValuedFlat.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Set
              is
              %strong flat
              if the opposite of its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(C)^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
          %p
            For disambiguation with the later notions, we may refer to such a functor as being
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                \-valued flat
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Spelled out explicitly, this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E : C \to Set
              is flat precisely if the following three conditions hold.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (non-emptiness) There is at least one
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(c)
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
              %li
                %p
                  (transitivity) For objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c,d \in C
                  and elements
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in E(c)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in E(d)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in C
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo :
                          %mi b
                          %mo →
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : b \to c
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : b \to d
                  and an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in E(b)
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi w
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\alpha) : w \mapsto y
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi β
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi w
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\beta) :w \mapsto z
              %li
                %p
                  (freeness) For two parallel morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi β
                        %mo :
                        %mi c
                        %mo →
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta : c \to d
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in E(c)
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi β
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\alpha)(y) = E(\beta)(y)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : b \to c
                  and an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in E(b)
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi γ
                        %mo =
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \circ \gamma = \beta \circ \gamma
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi z
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\gamma) : z \mapsto y
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to Set
              is
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set] \to Set
              preserves finite limits.
          %p
            This partially explains the terminology “flat”, since the Yoneda extension is a sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+functors"} tensoring with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat module
            is one such that tensoring with it preserves finite limits.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to Set
              is flat, then it preserves all finite limits that exist in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has finite limits and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves them, then it is flat.
          %h3#representable_flatness Representable flatness
          #RepresentablyFlat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C \rightarrow E
              is
              %strong flat
              if for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e / F)^{op}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e/F)
            is equivalent to the category of elements of the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi e
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \xrightarrow{F} E \xrightarrow{E(e,-)} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(e,F-)\colon C\to Set
            is Set-valued flat for every
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\in E
            = succeed "." do
              %strong representably flat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\in E
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                There is an object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                and a morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\to F(c)
            %li
              %p
                For any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c,d\in C
                and morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi e
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:e\to F(c)
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo :
                        %mi e
                        %mo →
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z:e\to F(d)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo :
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : b \to c
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : b \to d
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mi e
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w: e\to F(b)
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi w
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\alpha)\circ w = y
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi w
                        %mo =
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\beta)\circ w = z
            %li
              %p
                For two parallel morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ,
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta : c \to d
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi e
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y : e \to F(c)
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\alpha)\circ y = F(\beta)\circ y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo :
                      %mi b
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : b \to c
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %mi e
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z : e \to F(b)
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi γ
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \circ \gamma = \beta \circ \gamma
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi z
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\gamma) \circ z = y
          %p
            Representably flat functors are sometimes referred to simply as “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"}> left exact functors
            ”. On the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to E
              between small categories is representably flat if and only if the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_F\colon [C^{op}, Set] \to [E^{op},Set]
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              preserves finite limits.
          %p
            A proof of this is given below as prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlatnessIfYonedaExtensionPreservesFiniteLimits"}
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is representably flat, then it preserves all finite limits that exist in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has finite limits and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves them, then it is representably flat.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has finite limits, then a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Set
              is representably flat if and only if it is Set-valued flat, if and only if it preserves finite limits.
          %p
            However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            lacks finite limits, then representable flatness of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Set
            can be stronger than Set-valued flatness.
          %h3#ToposValuedFlatFunctors Topos-valued functors
          #InternallyFlat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              (for instance a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is
              %strong flat
              if the statement “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed ".\u201D" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SetValuedFlat"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              Explicitly, this means that for any finite diagram
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\colon I\to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim (F\circ D)
              of the
              = succeed "-images" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphic
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            For disambiguation, this notion of flatness may be called
            %strong internally flat
            since it refers to the internal logic of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %ul
            %li
              In
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"} Johnstone, C2.3.7 and B3.2.3
              they are called “torsors”.
            %li
              In
              %a{:href => "#MLM"} Mac Lane-Moerdijk, VII.8
              they are called “filtering functors”.
            %li
              In
              %a{:href => "#Moerdijk"} Moerdijk, II.2
              they are called “principal functors”.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since the internal logic of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              is just ordinary logic, a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Set
              is internally flat just when it is
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SetValuedFlat"}
          %p More generally:
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is internally flat precisely if for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalks"} stalks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* : E \to Set
              the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* \circ F
              is
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              In a topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              with enough points, a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* f
              is an epimorphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalks"} stalks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* : E \to Set
              commute with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is internally flat if and only if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set] \to E
              preserves finite limits.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_4 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is internally flat, then it preserves all finite limits that exist in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has finite limits and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves them, then it is internally flat.
          %h3#SiteValuedFunctors Site-valued functors
          %p
            Finally, we can give the most general definition, due to
            %a{:href => "#Karazeris"} Karazeris
          #CoveringFlat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              be any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is
              %strong flat
              if for any finite diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\colon I\to C
              and any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ D
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              with vertex
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi v
                    %mo →
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi T
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mtext factors through the
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mtext -image of some cone over
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ h\colon v\to u | T h \,\text{ factors through the }\, F\text{-image of some cone over }\, D \}
            %p
              is a covering sieve of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            For disambiguation, we may refer to this notion as being
            = succeed "." do
              %strong covering-flat
          %p This subsumes the other three definitions as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E=Set
                with its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+topology"} canonical topology
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SetValuedFlat"}
            %li
              %p
                More generally, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is a cocomplete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                with its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+topology"} canonical topology
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternallyFlat"}
            %li
              %p
                On the other hand, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+topology"} trivial topology
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RepresentablyFlat"}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a small category and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small-generated+site"} small-generated site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to E
              is covering-flat if and only if its extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set] \to Sh(E)
              preserves finite limits.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_5 Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is covering-flat, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              has finite limits and all covering families in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+epimorphism"} extremal-epic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves all finite limits that exist in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has finite limits and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              preserves them, then it is covering-flat.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#yoneda_extensions Yoneda extensions
          %p We now prove the asserted propositions about the equivalence of flatness with finite-limit-preserving extensions to presheaf categories.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to Set
              is Set-valued flat if and only if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set] \to Set
              preserves finite limits.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              This is prop. 6.3.8 in (
              %a{:href => "#Borceux"}> Borceux
              ).
          #FlatnessIfYonedaExtensionPreservesFiniteLimits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to E
              is representably flat if and only if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_F\colon [C^{op}, Set] \to [E^{op},Set]
              preserves finite limits.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo !
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_! = Lan_F
              is computed on any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
              (as discussed at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi F
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %mi Set
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F_! X(e) = \lim_{\to} \left( (e/F)^{op} \to C^{op} \stackrel{X}{\to} Set \right)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e/F)
              is the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e/F)^{op} \to C^{op}
              is the canonical projection.
            %p
              Now, by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              being representably-flat means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi F
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e/F)^{op}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a cocomplete topos, a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
              is internally flat if and only if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set] \to E
              preserves finite limits.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              This is VII.9.1 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#MLM"} Mac Lane-Moerdijk
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a sheaf topos, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C\to E
            is internally flat, then the restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set] \to E
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            still preserves finite limits, and it is cocontinuous just when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            preserves covering families. Since cocontinuous left-exact functors between sheaf toposes are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            parts of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            characterise geometric morphisms into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for such functors. This can be very useful when a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            has a presentation by a particularly simple site.
          %h3#CategoryOfFlatFunctors Category of flat functors
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FlatFunc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  FlatFunc(A^{op}, Set) \subset Func(A^{op}, Set)
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-objects"} ind-objects
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FlatFunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FlatFunc(A^{op},Set)
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              precisely if for every finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#KarazerisVelebil"}> KarazerisVelebil
            ).
          %h3#DiaconescuTheorem Classifying toposes and Diaconescu’s theorem
          %p
            The following statement is known as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternallyFlat"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to \mathcal{E}
            are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+images"} inverse images
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Diaconescu’s theorem)
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi FlatFunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Topos(\mathcal{E}, PSh(C))
                    \\simeq
                    FlatFunc(C, \mathcal{E})
            %p
              between the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \mathcal{E} \to PSh(C)
              and the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internally+flat+functors"} internally flat functors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to \mathcal{E}
            %p
              This equivalence takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \stackrel{j}{\to} PSh(C) \stackrel{f^*}{\to} \mathcal{E}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            One says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
            is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for internally flat functors out of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+sites"} Morphisms of sites
                are flat functors which additionally preserve covering families.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat module
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+flat+functors"} theory of flat functors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} flat (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-object
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Borceux
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              , Section 6.3 in:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
              Vol. 1:
              %em Basic Category Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525858"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525858
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p In
          %ul#Johnstone
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
              \.
          %p internally flat functors (“torsors”) are discussed around B3.2, and representably flat functors around C2.3.7.
          %p In
          %ul#MLM
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"} Saunders Mac Lane
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
              \.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            \-valued flat functors are discussed in VII.6, and internally flat functors in VII.8 (both called “filtering functors”).
          %p In section 2 of
          %ul#Moerdijk
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying spaces and classifying topoi
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1616
          %p internally flat functors with values in a topos with enough points are discussed.
          %p For the relationship between the various notions of flatness, and the notion of covering-flatness, see
          %ul#Karazeris
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Panagis+Karazeris"}> Panagis Karazeris
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notions of flatness relative to a Grothendieck topology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/12/5/12-05abs.html"} TAC
          %ul#Shulman
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2011/06/flat_functors_and_morphisms_of.html"} Flat Functors and Morphisms of Sites
          %p Limits in the category of flat functors are discussed in
          %ul#KarazerisVelebil
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Panagis+Karazeris"}> Panagis Karazeris
              , Jiří Velebil,
              %em Representability relative to a doctrine
              , Cahiers de Topologie et Géometrie Différentielle Catégoriques 50 (2009), 3–22.
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functors"} left exact functors
            or flat functors in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , def. 5.3.2.1 in
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            On flat
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giacomo+Tendas"} Giacomo Tendas
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat vs. filtered colimits in the enriched context
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.08612"} arXiv:2107.08612
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2022.108381"} doi
          %p
            On flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            in the broader context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category theory
            with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
